# Keep line endings stable across machines. Without this, committing from a
# Windows checkout rewrites whole files as CRLF and buries real changes: the
# "Fixes" commit touched 4 files but reported ~3400 changed lines in
# chessboard.rs alone, all of it line-ending churn.
#
# Existing files are left alone until someone runs `git add --renormalize .`;
# doing that in its own commit keeps it out of the way of real diffs.
* text=auto eol=lf
